request: Add a button that clears every movie whose `seen` flag is true from the watchlist.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist-store, watchlist  (The request's "seen" flag corresponds to the codebase's existing `watched` boolean on WatchItem (the only seen/unseen marker, surfaced via watchedCount/toggleWatched). Two units change: watchlist-store gains a `clearWatched()` mutation, and the watchlist view gains a "Clear watched" button that calls it. No other unit needs to change.)
round 1: owners watchlist-store=ok watchlist=ok; oracle RED
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 1 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist-store, watchlist  (Both oracle failures were in my acceptance-test harnesses, not in the units: the watchlist spec lacked router providers (NG0201 for RouterLink), and the watchlist-store spec's try/catch TestBed fallback crashed when constructing a second instance within one test. Shipping corrected harnesses for both units; the new store harness also verifies clearWatched persistence directly (including the empty-list case), so any real persistence bug surfaces cleanly next round.)
round 2: owners watchlist-store=ok watchlist=ok; oracle RED
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 1 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 3: plan -> watchlist-store  (Only remaining failure is watchlist-store's clearWatched persistence contract: after add -> toggleWatched -> clearWatched, a brand-new store loads [] instead of the unwatched remainder [2], while in-memory state after clearWatched is correct. So what reaches localStorage across that chain is empty or unloadable. tsc and all other 44 tests (including the watchlist Clear-watched button) are green; only watchlist-store needs to change.)
round 3: owners watchlist-store=ok; oracle RED
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 2 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 4: plan -> watchlist-store  (The build is red solely because of two TS7006 implicit-any errors on lambda parameter 'm' in the watchlist-store owner's own spec file (lines 242 and 303); vitest's angular-compiler plugin fails on them so no tests ran last round. Annotating those two parameters is a compile-only fix that unblocks the suite — including the already-written acceptance tests for clearWatched persistence and the Clear watched button — with no interface or behavior changes needed.)

